/speckit.plan

Technical direction for Feature 001:

- ASP.NET Core / C# backend
- EF Core for persistence abstraction
- SQLite for the pilot/V1 provider
- Keep persistence portable for possible SQL Server/PostgreSQL later
- Manual/controlled Excel input for this feature
- Use a header-driven common ingestion pipeline; no DR-specific parsers
- Separate Excel reading, validation, normalization, domain logic, persistence,
  diagnostics and activation so they are independently testable
- Preserve last-known-good dataset through atomic activation
- Include automated compatibility tests against representative RLLOT workbooks
- No React/dashboard UI, SharePoint automation or scheduling in Feature 001

Use the clarified spec.md and constitution as the source of truth.
Surface any remaining technical uncertainty instead of guessing.